<article class="env-lemma" id="0AXR">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AXR">Lemma <span data-tag="0AXR">31.11.1</span>.</a> Let $X$ be an integral scheme with generic point $\eta $. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a quasi-coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Let $U \subset X$ be nonempty open and $s \in \mathcal{F}(U)$. The following are equivalent </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
for some $x \in U$ the image of $s$ in $\mathcal{F}_ x$ is torsion, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for all $x \in U$ the image of $s$ in $\mathcal{F}_ x$ is torsion, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the image of $s$ in $\mathcal{F}_\eta $ is zero, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the image of $s$ in $j_*\mathcal{F}_\eta $ is zero, where $j : \eta \to X$ is the inclusion morphism. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>